WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.470
A lake in the wind.

2
00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:06.280
"I wandered lonely as a
cloud", the poem begins.

3
00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:10.410
Then, all at once, a
crowd of golden daffodils.

4
00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:14.660
Thousands of them, fluttering
and dancing beside the lake.

5
00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:17.380
But the last stanza is indoors.

6
00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:19.160
He's lying on his couch.

7
00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:21.720
And that is where the poem ends.

8
00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:25.290
A poem about daffodils
that ends on a couch.

9
00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:27.030
Why end there?

10
00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:30.350
In this mission, you'll go
back to the walk by Ullswater,

11
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:34.390
on 15 April 1802, that the poem grew from.

12
00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:37.710
You'll pin down what
changes in the final stanza:

13
00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:39.720
where he is, and when.

14
00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:43.870
And you'll see how Wordsworth
makes the flowers seem alive.

15
00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:47.880
Your mission: explain why
the poem ends on a couch.
